<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Sharif al-Murtada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">965–1044</span> · Also known as Sharif al-Murtada</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Sharif al-Murtada was a Twelver Shia theologian, jurist and poet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, a descendant of the Prophet through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">Imam</a> Musa al-Kazim and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-sharif-al-radi">al-Sharif al-Radi</a>. He succeeded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-shaykh-al-mufid">al-Shaykh al-Mufid</a> as the leading Shia scholar of the city and led the Talibid descendants of Ali under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyids</a>. His works shaped Shia rational theology and legal theory.</p></div>
